      "narrative": "Elmstead County file abbreviated accounts, so there is no public profit and loss account: revenue, wages and the annual result are not disclosed. What the balance sheet does show is a club that has slipped into negative net assets. Liabilities of £18.7m now exceed assets of £17.6m, leaving net liabilities of £1.1m, after net assets fell in every year from £3.2m in 2020.\n\nThe accounts carry a going concern warning, and the short-term position explains why. Current liabilities of £8.4m are close to twice current assets of £4.6m, cash is £2.1m, and borrowing has grown from £4.2m to £6.5m over five years. Without the profit and loss figures we can't work out a distress score, but the balance sheet alone places the club among the division's weakest.\n\nOn the pitch the club is fifth, and transfer activity has been close to neutral, at £0.8m of net spend over three years. The steady fall in net assets suggests continuing losses, funded by rising debt. The next set of accounts will show whether that trend has been stopped.",
