      "narrative": "Hollowfield United have the highest distress score in the division, and the accounts carry a going concern warning. Wages of £20.9m now exceed revenue of £19.3m, total costs of £29.5m produced an operating loss of £10.2m, and finance costs of £1.9m helped take the net loss to £11.3m.\n\nThe balance sheet has worsened every year. Net liabilities have grown from £1.5m in 2020 to £42.3m, with total liabilities of £64.6m against assets of £22.3m. Debt has more than doubled to £42.0m over the same period, cash is £0.9m, and current liabilities are more than five times current assets. The distress score is 100, the maximum.\n\nRevenue has fallen in each of the last four years, from £22.0m to £19.3m, while the wage bill has held at around £21m. The club is bottom of the table despite the fourth-largest payroll, four places below where that spending should put it. It depends on new money from its owners or lenders to keep trading.",
